1	//! jj backend — the ONLY site that touches `jj-lib`.
2	//!
3	//! Most reads (`log_page`, `changeset`, `current_ref`) are read-only: they `open` the workspace and
4	//! `load_at_head`, reading commit data WITHOUT snapshotting/locking the working copy (prior learning
5	//! `jj-concurrent-probes-working-copy-lock`: jj takes the working-copy lock only on ops that *write*
6	//! `@`). The exception is `working_status` (`snapshot_working_copy`), which MUST snapshot `@` so it
7	//! reflects on-disk edits — so it takes the lock + rewrites `@`, exactly like every `jj` command.
8	//!
9	//! Two different ref reads live here, and they are NOT interchangeable: `bookmark_map` reads LOCAL
10	//! bookmarks (the history rows' labels), while `origin_tips` reads the tracked bookmarks on remote
11	//! `origin` (push state). Never mix them — see `PUSH_REMOTE` for why counting jj's pseudo-remote `git`
12	//! would report every local commit as pushed.
