50	/// Classify a `Workspace::load` failure instead of flattening it to `Io`, so the app can tell
51	/// "this isn't a jj repo (any more)" from "we can't read this repo". Each arm reaches a distinct
52	/// Swift `VCSError` case and from there a distinct UI state — see `RustJJProvider.mapError`.
53	///
54	/// - the two "no repo at this path" variants → `UnsupportedRepo`: the `.jj` dir (or the `repo` dir a
55	///   secondary workspace's `.jj/repo` file points at) is gone, so the path the app has registered as
56	///   a jj project no longer is one. Swift maps this to the sidebar's "not a repository", the same
57	///   honest answer git already gives.
58	/// - `StoreLoadError::UnsupportedType` → `BackendVersion`: the repo names a backend (commit / op /
59	///   index / working-copy store) that this build's `StoreFactories` doesn't know — the signature of a
60	///   repo written by a newer jj than the `jj-lib` we pin. Retrying can't help; the message names the
61	///   store and type so the user can see which.
62	/// - everything else (unreadable paths, undecodable repo path, working-copy state, other store load
63	///   failures) stays `Io`: a real I/O-shaped failure with nothing more specific to say.
64	fn workspace_load_err(e: WorkspaceLoadError) -> VcsError {
65	    match e {
66	        WorkspaceLoadError::NoWorkspaceHere(path) => {
67	            VcsError::UnsupportedRepo(format!("no jj repo at {}", path.display()))
68	        }
69	        WorkspaceLoadError::RepoDoesNotExist(path) => {
70	            VcsError::UnsupportedRepo(format!("jj repo no longer at {}", path.display()))
71	        }
72	        WorkspaceLoadError::StoreLoadError(StoreLoadError::UnsupportedType {
73	            store,
74	            store_type,
75	        }) => VcsError::BackendVersion(format!("unsupported {store} backend type '{store_type}'")),
76	        other => io(other),
77	    }
78	}
