76	/// A repo whose `@` is a 2-sided **modify/modify** conflict on `f.txt`:
77	/// `base` → (`left`, `right`) → `jj new <left> <right>`. `@`'s first parent is `left`, so a tree diff
78	/// of `@` vs its first parent yields `f.txt` with an unresolved `after` value.
79	///
80	/// The two sides are addressed by **commit id**, never by bookmark: with jj's
81	/// `experimental-advance-branches` enabled, `jj commit` advances a bookmark onto the commit it just
82	/// created, which collapses the two sides onto one and produces no conflict at all. (`init_repo`'s
83	/// isolated `JJ_CONFIG` already keeps that setting out of these tests, but ids don't depend on it.)
84	///
85	/// Built with the `jj` CLI on PATH while the read under test is `jj-lib =0.43.0`. That skew is
86	/// expected to be harmless, but if this fixture ever breaks on CI first, suspect the CLI before the
87	/// classifier.
88	fn conflicted_repo(tag: &str) -> (PathBuf, PathBuf) {
89	    let (dir, cfg) = init_repo(tag);
